==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Team Flare Grunt Adventures.png|thumb|230px|A male and female Grunt in Pokémon Adventures]]
Team Flare Grunts made their debut in ''[[PS550|X-actly What They Wanted]]''. They have been frequently used to attack {{adv|X}} and his friends in order to obtain X's [[Mega Ring]] to power Team Flare's ultimate weapon.

Team Flare Grunts were also stationed at [[Cyllage City]]; they recaptured {{kal|Grace}} a number of times.

The Team Flare Grunt that owns a Tyrunt and four Espurr was set the task of obtaining [[Mega Stone]]s compiled in a list; after losing the Manectite to X, he also lost this list to X and {{adv|Trevor}}. 

Later, [[Sina]] and [[Dexio]] arrived at [[Lysandre Café]], having knocked out a grunt and sent information to [[Professor Sycamore]] about Team Flare's core group at [[Pokémon Village]]. According to [[Xerosic]], Grunts were stationed on the routes around the [[Pokémon Village]] to stop X and his allies from advancing to the village, but [[Wikstrom]], [[Siebold]], and [[Drasna]] of the [[Elite Four]] overwhelmed them. At around the same time, [[Gym Leader]]s [[Grant]], [[Ramos]], [[Olympia]], [[Valerie]] and [[Wulfric]] defeated the Grunts stationed at Cyllage City.

